        <li>Modify it however you like, including removing every trace of us.</li>
        <li>Hand the modified site to a client as part of paid work.</li>
        <li>Keep using it forever. The licence does not expire or renew.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="divider">

      <h3>What you may not do</h3>
      <ul class="stack mt-2">
        <li>Resell or redistribute <b>the template itself</b>, modified or not.</li>
        <li>Include it in another template, theme, or template bundle.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr class="divider">

      <p class="small muted">
        That's the entire licence. Building a second site means a second <%= money(store.templatePriceCents) %>, which is
        the only catch and we think a fair one. Questions:
        <a href="mailto:<%= store.supportEmail %>"><%= store.supportEmail %></a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
